# All visualizations are dark mode, always

Every visualization created in this project — inline HTML fragments,
self-contained HTML files, `html_preview` / `html_render` output, diagrams and
infographics — MUST be dark mode. Never produce a light-mode visual.

Rules:
- Use a dark canvas (`#141414` or equivalent), dark panels (`#1e1e1e`),
  light text (`#F7F5F0`), muted gray secondary text (`#A8A297`),
  subtle dark borders (`#34312D`).
- The only accent is flame orange `#FF6A00`, used for active/clickable states
  and highlights. No blue, green, teal, purple, gradients, glassmorphism or
  bright backgrounds.
- Call `html_preview` with `appearance: "dark"` every time.
- When writing a standalone HTML file for `html_render`, include its own CSS;
  do not rely on host-only classes such as `.vis-card` or `.vis-chart-meta`,
  because those render as plain text outside the chat host.
- Keep the dark palette even if the surrounding application or another tool
  defaults to light mode. Dark mode is the permanent default for visuals.
